{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_015WdVqHGmfsagT2oeCJMSA7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Summary of build trio session **rnd-v1** (Anchor R&D Control Surface v1 â€” Foreman-built, all waves dated 2026-06-08):\n\n- **Wave 2 â€” Foundations (code only):** Added `paths.py` (lazy `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR` resolution, `ensure_data_dirs()`, process-wide re-entrant `WRITE_LOCK`, `auth_ok()`/`expected_token()`, `bind_with_retry()`, idempotent `migrate_data()`); moved `anchor_gui.py` to `ThreadingHTTPServer` with `@_with_write_lock` on all mutators, a token gate atop `do_POST`, and `make_server()`; routed `anchor.py`/`anchor_healthcheck.py` paths through `paths`. Gate GREEN (22 passed) after 1 fix iteration.\n\n- **Wave 3 â€” Registry + New Project flow + per-project store + folder-grouped window:** Added `rnd_registry.py` (id-keyed, non-unique `folder_path`, CRUD + `group_by_folder` + retain-not-delete lifecycle + scaffolding of `.anchor/projects/<id>/{research,planning,build,deliverables,jobs}/` + tracking-policy `.gitignore`/README + idempotent legacy-id assignment; JSON under `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR`, writes under `paths.WRITE_LOCK`) and `dir_browser.py` (stdlib server-side dir browser). Added the New-Project flow, `/project/<id>` route, and folder-grouped tiles with a 4-state status line. GO after 1 fix iteration.\n\n- **Wave 4 â€” Mock runner + launch/tail primitive (durable-job keystone):** Added `job_runner.py` (`ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`-indirected launch; durable per-job log + ring buffer [deque maxlen 5000]; `long_poll(?since=K, ceiling=25s)`; `cancel()` via `taskkill /T /F /PID` setting status `cancelled` before kill; `liveness_check`/`reconcile_on_startup` â†’ `interrupted`; atomic tmpâ†’replace writes under `paths.WRITE_LOCK`) plus `tests/fake_claude.py` deterministic mock. GO with 0 fix iterations.\n\n- **Wave 5 â€” Gate adapter (in-session answers):** Added `gate_adapter.py` (parse stream-json â†’ prompt-box record `{question, options, tool_use_id, header, multiSelect}`; `mark_awaiting_input` persists `state=awaiting-input`). Authored a faithful deterministic stream-json gate fixture (`tests/fixtures/gate_stream.jsonl`, 6-line valid jsonl with a real `AskUserQuestion` tool_use) because the captured `crucible_gate.jsonl` was absent â€” no live claude. GO after 1 fix iteration.\n\n- **Wave 6 â€” Lane wiring + concurrency:** Added `lanes.py` (frozen lane map researchâ†’researchPrime / planâ†’crucible / buildâ†’foreman â†’ {skill, prompt-seed, output subdir, gate flag}; `launch_lane()` resolves project from registry, scaffolds + passes per-project output dir into the engine via `--skill/--output-dir/--prompt-seed`, writes a `launch.pointer.json` as on-disk proof; research no-gate, plan/build gate-in-session) and a `job_runner.py` concurrency layer (`_ACTIVE_LANE` keyed `(project_id,lane)` for same-lane serialize/cross-lane concurrent, `_FOLDER_BUILD` keyed `folder_path`). GO with 0 fix iterations.\n\n- **Wave 7 â€” Versioned history + report viewer + cost rollup + auto-commit:** Added `effort_history.py` (job-id-scoped pointer-records under `.anchor/projects/<id>/<lane>/efforts/`; append-only index reversed on read [index 0 newest, nothing deleted on re-run]; cost capture from result envelope; per-effortâ†’laneâ†’project rollups; per-effort scoped git auto-commit `git -C <folder>`, no push/global) and `report_viewer.py` (PDF-by-default when `report.pdf` present, else stdlib mdâ†’HTML Reader linking vendored KaTeX with auto-render; traversal-safe static serve). Vendored real KaTeX 0.16.11 (`katex.min.js` 275KB + css + auto-render + PROVENANCE). GO after 1 fix iteration.\n\n- **Wave 8 â€” Shareable, data-free distribution:** Added `distro.py` (deny-by-default manifest staging + no-personal-data scan), `dist_manifest.txt`, planted-secret fixtures, and `test_distro_scan`. Initial gate GREEN (117 passed) but **both independent refute-reviewers returned NO-GO**: BLOCKER-1 â€” `distro.py` hard-coded the real email literal `john.liechty@gmail.com` and shipped it (PII leak, passing only via a self-suppression marker); MAJOR-1 â€” the `distro-scan: allow` marker was globally exploitable (any staged file could self-grant a leak, reproduced end-to-end); MAJOR-2 â€” the token scan missed unquoted secrets.\n\n- **Wave 9 â€” Deliverables + taskâ†”project activation (TERMINAL wave):** Added `deliverables.py` (launch+watch with per-type success contracts: doc=exists+nonempty via `report_viewer`; script/skill=exit 0 AND result-no-error via `is_error` envelope check; program=exit 0 within timeout; enforces stdin=DEVNULL + non-interactive + execution timeout + tree-kill reap â†’ clean timeout, no orphan). Added the project-tasks view (filter by parsed `Project:` field), deliverables render, and token-gated `/api/rnd/link_task` & `/api/rnd/run_deliverable` to `anchor_gui.py`, plus `link_task`/`link` CLI to `anchor.py`. GO with 0 fix iterations.\n\n**Cross-cutting grounded facts:** every wave was executed and gated on 2026-06-08; the build followed an EXECUTE â†’ ADVERSARIAL-REVIEW (2 independent refute reviewers) â†’ FIX â†’ GATE loop; the runner was always indirected through the `ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`/`fake_claude.py` seam (no live claude); all data writes were serialized under `paths.WRITE_LOCK`.\n\n**Errors/findings of note:** Wave 8's clean test gate (117 passed) masked three real distribution-security defects that only the adversarial review caught â€” a shipped PII literal and two exploitable scan-bypass holes â€” none surfaced by the passing tests."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4276,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":94068,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d04b65e-e2